.TH GIT-QC 1 2026-09-24 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-qc \- commit, sync with the remote branch, and optionally push
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git qc
.RB [ p | \-p | \-\-push ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ message ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Like
.BR git\-c (1),
then, if the branch exists on the remote, rebase it onto the remote copy.
With
.BR p ,
push afterwards.
.PP
The commit happens before the sync: syncing first would autostash, and git
restores an autostash without the staged/unstaged split, so a partial
.B git add
would be lost.
.PP
Only
.BR p ,
.B \-p
and
.B \-\-push
select push mode; the word "push" starts the message like any other. Use
.B \-\-
before a message whose first word is "p".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-c (1),
.BR git\-ps (1),
.BR git\-workflow (7)
